  /**
     * ## FHI Segmented Control
 * 
 * https://designsystem.fhi.no/?path=/docs/komponenter-segmented-control--docs
 * 
 * The <fhi-segmented-control> component lets the user select one option from a group of related choices. Each choice is defined with a <fhi-segmented-control-item> element.
 * 
 * The choice should affect the content within the same context.
 * 
 * Example usage:
 * ```html
 * <fhi-segmented-control value="item2">
 *   <fhi-segmented-control-item value="item1">Item 1</fhi-segmented-control-item>
 *   <fhi-segmented-control-item value="item2">Item 2</fhi-segmented-control-item>
 *   <fhi-segmented-control-item value="item3">Item 3</fhi-segmented-control-item>
 * </fhi-segmented-control>
 * ```
 * 
 * ## Attributes & Properties
 * 
 * Component attributes and properties that can be applied to the element or by using JavaScript.
 * 
 * - `value`: The currently selected value of the segmented control. 
 * - `variant`: The visual style of the segmented control. This will be applied to all segmented control items within the group. 
 * 
 * ## Events
 * 
 * Events that will be emitted by the component.
 * 
 * - `change`: Standard DOM event with the type `change`.
 * This event is dispatched when the selected item of the segmented control changes.
 * 
 * ## Slots
 * 
 * Areas where markup can be added to the component.
 * 
 * - `(default)`: The default slot. Used for placing <fhi-segmented-control-item> elements.
  */
    "fhi-segmented-control": Partial<FhiSegmentedControlProps & BaseProps<FhiSegmentedControl> & BaseEvents>;


  /**
     * ## FHI Select Item
 * 
 * https://designsystem.fhi.no/?path=/docs/komponenter-select--docs
 * 
 * The `<fhi-select-item>` component is used to represent an individual option within a `<fhi-select>` dropdown list.
 * It provides a labeled option element with selection state and value attribute.
 * 
 * ## Attributes & Properties
 * 
 * Component attributes and properties that can be applied to the element or by using JavaScript.
 * 
 * - `label`: The label attribute of the select item. This property is used to provide a descriptive label for the select item. If not provided, the content of the `value` attribute will be used instead. 
 * - `selected`: The selected attribute of the select item. This property is used to indicate whether the select item is selected or not. 
 * - `value`: The value attribute of the select item. This property is used to identify the select item when submitting a form. If not provided, the text content will be used instead. 
 * 
 * ## Slots
 * 
 * Areas where markup can be added to the component.
 * 
 * - `(default)`: The default slot is used to provide text content for the `<fhi-select-item>` element.
  */
    "fhi-select-item": Partial<FhiSelectItemProps & BaseProps<FhiSelectItem> & BaseEvents>;


  /**
     * ## FHI Select
 * 
 * https://designsystem.fhi.no/?path=/docs/komponenter-select--docs
 * 
 * The `<fhi-select>` component is used to create a dropdown list of options for users to choose from.
 * It provides a labeled select element (`fhi-select-item`) with optional placeholder text, status indication, and a message area for additional information or validation feedback.
 * 
 * ## Attributes & Properties
 * 
 * Component attributes and properties that can be applied to the element or by using JavaScript.
 * 
 * - `disabled`: The disabled attribute of the select element. This property is used to disable the select element. 
 * - `help-text`/`helpText`: The message shown above the Select.
 * This is often used to provide additional information to the user. 
 * - `label`: The label attribute of the select element. This property is used to provide a descriptive label for the select element. 
 * - `message`: The message attribute of the select element. This property is used to provide a validation message for the select element. 
 * - `name`: The name attribute of the select element. This property is used to identify the select element when submitting a form. 
 * - `status`: The status attribute of the select element. This property is used to indicate the validation status of the select element. 
 * - `value`: The value attribute of the select element. This property is used to identify the selected option when submitting a form. 
 * - `selectElement`: undefined (property only)
 * - `slotElements`: undefined (property only)
 * 
 * ## Events
 * 
 * Events that will be emitted by the component.
 * 
 * - `change`: Standard DOM event with the type `change`.
 * This event is dispatched when the chosen option of the select changes.
 * - `input`: Standard DOM event with the type `input`.
 * This event is dispatched when the chosen option of the select changes.
 * 
 * ## Slots
 * 
 * Areas where markup can be added to the component.
 * 
 * - `(default)`: The default slot is used to provide the options for the select element. Each option should be represented by a `<fhi-select-item>` element.
 * 
 * ## Methods
 * 
 * Methods that can be called to access component functionality.
 * 
 * - `formResetCallback() => void`: undefined
  */
